import{_ as t,o as a,c as s,a2 as n}from"./chunks/framework.BUOFcz_J.js";const u=JSON.parse('{"title":"Claude, Codex and external ACP sessions","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"records/acp-multi-agent-episode.md","filePath":"records/acp-multi-agent-episode.md"}'),i={name:"records/acp-multi-agent-episode.md"};function o(r,e,d,l,c,p){return a(),s("div",null,[...e[0]||(e[0]=[n(`<div class="warning custom-block"><p class="custom-block-title">Historical record</p><p>This page records what happened on a date, with its observed failures and limits. It is not a requirement for the current implementation. Current behaviour is in <a href="/Rho/docs/reference/status">Status</a>.</p></div><h1 id="claude-codex-and-external-acp-sessions" tabindex="-1">Claude, Codex and external ACP sessions <a class="header-anchor" href="#claude-codex-and-external-acp-sessions" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Claude, Codex and external ACP sessions&quot;">​</a></h1><p>The 2026-10-27 request extended the first shared-workspace loop with a second Agent, external ACP sessions and fresh installation acceptance. Changes were implemented together, then verified and committed as one batch per owner. Westlake HPC remained the model provider. Core source and its selected binary were not changed or rebuilt.</p><h2 id="implemented-ownership" tabindex="-1">Implemented ownership <a class="header-anchor" href="#implemented-ownership" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Implemented ownership&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Agent 0.4.10 shares the ACP v1 connection driver between Claude and Codex, with provider-specific executable/configuration wrappers. Claude remains on adapter 0.97.0; Codex uses the official <code>@agentclientprotocol/codex-acp</code> 2.3.0 and its native Codex 0.164.0. Rho&#39;s new-conversation selector records the chosen backend under the original message identity. Retry, a changed default and restart cannot migrate that conversation to another Agent.</p><p>Connection-level plans, usage, titles and tool references feed the same Project work surface and Documents notes owner. Standard ACP diff paths are also file references, without retaining old/new file contents. Current file hashes remain independent observations; they do not establish authorship or domain correctness. Normal shutdown uses advertised <code>session/close</code> before ending the owned transport. Process-group escalation remains active even after the adapter wrapper exits.</p><p>An external client selects <code>rho --acp /absolute/project --acp-agent codex</code> (<code>claude</code> is also supported) as its Agent command. It can load an existing native session. The relay forwards unchanged stdio bytes, observing only the selected project into <code>.rho/agent/acp/</code>. Input, permissions and runtime lifetime stay in the original client. Project work reads the same projection without starting an Agent or Host, with a separate <code>external-acp</code> source identity and sequence. Rho shutdown does not stop that external session. The visible work surface polls its own read every 1.5 seconds because external updates do not advance Rho&#39;s application cursor.</p><p>This accepts explicit ACP v1 relay attachment, not passive attachment to an uninstrumented running client. ACP v1 does not define that generic capability. Claude/dsh transcript collection remains the existing fallback; it is neither removed nor relabelled as ACP. External-session real-model acceptance here uses Codex; the Claude relay branch has component coverage.</p><h2 id="verification-setup-and-failures-retained" tabindex="-1">Verification setup and failures retained <a class="header-anchor" href="#verification-setup-and-failures-retained" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Verification setup and failures retained&quot;">​</a></h2><p>Node 22.22.3 and Chrome 155.0.8059.84 run disposable projects and owned processes. Credentials are read from existing local configuration into child environments; reports and source contain no gateway address or credential. Codex uses an isolated native home and a Responses provider named Westlake HPC with <code>westlakehpc/deepseek-v4.1-flash</code>, workspace-write mode, native <code>tools.update_plan.enabled=true</code> and <code>features.apply_patch_freeform=true</code>. The provider does not supply Codex model metadata; reported context capacity is native fallback metadata, not a verified Westlake context-window limit.</p><p>The batch exposed and retained these failures before final acceptance:</p><ul><li>Codex&#39;s native plan tool defaults off. The harness now explicitly enables it; prose is never converted into a fabricated ACP plan.</li><li>A real Codex cancelled response can leave a native shell command alive, even when the model requested a long foreground yield. The UI says the turn was cancelled and unfinished tools may still run. Codex checks record native PID state separately; any harness cleanup of its own gate is labelled, not counted as product termination evidence. Claude&#39;s foreground-exit evidence is separate.</li><li>Killing/closing only the adapter wrapper could leave native session ownership temporarily occupied. Advertised session close and complete owned-group shutdown address normal release; no competing writer is evicted or new session invented.</li><li>Codex emitted file paths in standard diff content without <code>locations</code>. The owner now retains those references, and tests ensure file contents are excluded.</li><li>A read immediately after Rho restart hit a stale HTTP socket. The external harness retries only that read, never a prompt or tool action.</li><li>One MCP test timed out under concurrent load, then passed alone. A later run overlapped generated/build output and failed to import incomplete modules. Those runs are not accepted; the completed-build application run passed all 192 tests, and the final Agent owner run passed all 89. Contract/type checks also passed.</li><li>Earlier live runs include a provider turn reaching the existing wall limit. Their partial/unknown/stopped results remain in the local reports.</li></ul><p>Detailed failed attempts are retained under <code>work/acp-codex-source*</code>, <code>work/acp-external-source*</code>, and <code>work/acp-multi-tests*.log</code>. Component evidence is <code>work/acp-multi-tests-verified.log</code>, <code>work/acp-multi-contracts-complete.log</code> and <code>work/acp-multi-final/owner-tests.log</code>. These checks do not establish human usability, all ACP update displays, a cross-resource revision or remote ACP transport support. The application still owns selection and linked observations; the model loop and native tool execution remain outside Rho.</p><h2 id="installed-acceptance" tabindex="-1">Installed acceptance <a class="header-anchor" href="#installed-acceptance" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Installed acceptance&quot;">​</a></h2><p>The selected unsigned local package is <code>work/acp-multi-final/rho-workspace-local-0.4.0.tgz</code>, SHA-256 <code>f9ce8435d134b7213bcd40e174abc985ab26e8af45a874ededcbcf8a5a811caf</code>. Its composition records explicit dirty-source build-input overrides; the final source association is recorded separately without altering the accepted tarball. Core is the digest-verified existing binary <code>434a92fced13595d281b1f9e2d6d49cf9fa7c8a451da08aa3c1ba86cec85eab3</code>. No Core build, source edit or Host startup was needed by these Agent episodes.</p><p>The package was installed at <code>/tmp/rho-acp-installed-h7aADQ</code>, outside all three source checkouts. Real-model harnesses resolved the service, clients, browser assets, Agent, ACP adapters and their SDK/native dependencies from that installed package. The same immutable artifact passed:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Check</th><th>Observed result</th><th>Local evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>CLI installation and startup</td><td>Passed; bundled Core digest matched; four viewport widths, zero remaining Hosts</td><td><code>work/acp-multi-install-smoke/report.json</code></td></tr><tr><td>Claude Code 2.1.311</td><td>Eight turns, nine checks; lost send ACK, shared context/MCP, browser loss, cancellation, transport loss, same-session load, Rho restart and saved human notes applied to result bytes</td><td><code>work/acp-installed-claude/report.json</code></td></tr><tr><td>Codex 0.164.0</td><td>Same eight-turn loop and nine checks, including native plan/file references and original permission choices</td><td><code>work/acp-installed-codex/report.json</code></td></tr><tr><td>External Codex ACP</td><td>Three checks; pre-existing external session loaded through relay, live plan/result observation during Rho restart, reconnect with unchanged identity/context and one gate invocation</td><td><code>work/acp-installed-external/report.json</code></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Both conversation sequences ended <code>completed, completed, completed, stopped, unknown, completed, completed, completed</code>. The interrupted fifth prompt was never replayed. Claude&#39;s cancelled foreground command exited. Codex&#39;s cancelled turn left its foreground gate alive (<code>Ss</code>); the harness explicitly sent SIGTERM to its own test PID and labelled that cleanup. This is accepted turn cancellation with an unconfirmed native job, not a claim that Codex stopped every native process.</p><p>Screenshots were inspected at desktop and phone sizes, including permission, unknown-outcome, notes and external-input states. Immediate work snapshots can still show the preceding state until the next bounded read. Read-only reload screens were captured after waiting for <code>Last message answered</code>, preserving the same session/version without starting an Agent. The documents editor&#39;s existing Claude-specific edit-toggle wording and raw Markdown transcript display remain UI limitations; this batch does not claim human usability.</p><p>To rerun against a separately installed package:</p><div class="language-sh vp-adaptive-theme"><button title="Copy Code" class="copy"></button><span class="lang">sh</span><pre class="shiki shiki-themes github-light github-light vp-code" tabindex="0"><code><span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6F42C1;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> scripts/acp-episode.mjs</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --agent</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> claude</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --work</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --package-root</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/install/node_modules/@rho-workspace/local</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6F42C1;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> scripts/acp-episode.mjs</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --agent</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> codex</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --work</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --package-root</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/install/node_modules/@rho-workspace/local</span></span>
<span class="line"><span style="--shiki-light:#6F42C1;--shiki-dark:#6F42C1;">node</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> scripts/acp-external-episode.mjs</span><span style="--shiki-light:#005CC5;--shiki-dark:#005CC5;"> --package-root</span><span style="--shiki-light:#032F62;--shiki-dark:#032F62;"> /absolute/install/node_modules/@rho-workspace/local</span></span></code></pre></div><p>Use <code>RHO_ACP_EVIDENCE</code> to select each report directory. The existing local provider configuration supplies credentials; no credential is required in these commands. These checks accept a local macOS arm64 npm artifact. Registry publication, signing, remote ACP transport and additional platforms remain separate.</p><h2 id="observation-limits" tabindex="-1">Observation limits <a class="header-anchor" href="#observation-limits" aria-label="Permalink to &quot;Observation limits&quot;">​</a></h2><p>External records retain at most 64 sessions, 512 KiB per record and 8,192 characters of the latest visible reply. Pending requests/permissions and pre-identity updates are each capped at 128; pre-identity bytes are capped at 512 KiB and parsed transport lines at 4 MiB. Projection failure keeps old evidence and allows the original transport to continue. Unsafe setup directories refuse before writing outside the project. A dead relay PID or expired ten-second heartbeat lease makes observations disconnected and unfinished outcomes unknown. Reads scan at most 256 entries. Project work shows at most eight external sessions (connected first, then recent), counts omissions and retains each source&#39;s own version. Existing plan/tool/file limits remain in the <a href="https://github.com/YuLab-SMU/Rho-plugins/blob/main/plugins/agent/README.md" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Agent README</a>.</p>`,24)])])}const m=t(i,[["render",o]]);export{u as __pageData,m as default};
